sections.body:
The Hub stores:
- your account: email, display name, the scrambled password, two-step sign-in settings, verification status, and which version of these terms you agreed to and when;
- the classes you make or join, your role in them, and your leaderboard name choice;
- your study answers and scores (to grade questions, schedule reviews and run leaderboards);
- files you choose to save to your Kea storage;
- security records: sign-ins, failed sign-ins and the network address they came from, kept to stop break-in attempts.
The Hub does not store payroll data such as Social Security numbers, bank account numbers or tax forms. Those stay encrypted on the payroll admin's own computer.
Your data is never sold, never used for ads, and never shared except as these terms describe (for example, with the classes and organizations you join) or when the law requires it.
Backups of the Hub are encrypted before they leave the Hub's computer.
